What is derived:

1. The fourteen definitions UMat, relativeUnitary, IsUnbiased, IsMUBFamily, HasMUBs, HasCompleteMUBs,
   IsMaxMUBCount (from FormalConjectures/OpenQuantumProblems/13.lean) and StateVector, IsNormalized, overlapSq,
   HasConstantOverlapSq, sicOverlapSq, IsSICFamily, HasSICPOVM (from FormalConjectures/OpenQuantumProblems/23.lean)
   in Challenge.lean and QuantumDesigns/Defs.lean are restated character for character, with the namespace changed
   and the docstrings kept.
2. Lemmas whose docstrings say "adapts ... of ..." are modified from those files; those docstrings are the
   modification notices. They are: in QuantumDesigns/Bound.lean, bd_proj, bd_vec, bd_inner_vec, bd_inner_proj,
   bd_inner_proj_same, bd_inner_proj_unbiased and bd_w (from colProjector, matToEuc, inner_matToEuc,
   colProjector_inner_eq_mul, colProjector_inner_self, colProjector_inner_diff, colProjector_inner_unbiased and
   dftProjector of the XC0R fork's OpenQuantumProblems/13.lean, with the sixth root of unity replaced by a primitive
   d-th root); in QuantumDesigns/Tensor.lean, tn_kroneckerUMat, tn_relativeUnitary_kronecker, tn_isUnbiased_kronecker
   and hasMUBs_mul_internal (from kroneckerUMat, relativeUnitary_kronecker, isUnbiased_kronecker and hasMUBs_mul of
   the same file); in QuantumDesigns/SIC.lean, hg_qubit and hg_hesse (from qubitSICFamily and hesseFamily of
   google-deepmind/formal-conjectures' OpenQuantumProblems/23.lean, restated with real parameters).

